# Formatting

## Indentation

- Use **2 spaces** only. Never tabs. Never 4 spaces.
- Do not mix indentation styles in the same file.

## Braces (same line)

Opening `{` stays on the **same line** as the statement that starts the block.

```typescript
// Correct
function save_profile() {
  if (is_valid) {
    return data;
  }
}

class Header {
  render() {
    return null;
  }
}

interface SiteConfig {
  title: string;
}

// Wrong
function save_profile()
{
  if (is_valid)
  {
    return data;
  }
}
```

Applies to: `function`, `if` / `else` / `for` / `while` / `switch`, `try` / `catch` / `finally`, `class`, `interface`, `type` object literals when multiline, and arrow functions only when the body is a block `{ ... }` (not single-expression `=>` without braces).

## Other

- Do not use single-line conditionals without braces (`if (x) return y;` with no `{ }` is discouraged when adding or editing control flow).
- Match surrounding file style when editing existing code; use these rules for new code and intentional formatting fixes.
